course: dictionary
lesson: 3546
title: Feeding: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feeding is a word with more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. Look for clues such as who or what is being fed, and when or where it happens.
explain: «Winter feeding helps small birds survive.» Here feeding means giving food to birds, not eating. Try the swap: "giving food helps small birds survive" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: «...which cuts down fights at feeding time.» Feeding time is the time when the piglets eat. Here feeding means eating, which is the second meaning. The same clue, time, tells you the sense.
explain: «...piglets double their birth weight in about a week.» In «every feed», feed means one meal. Ask yourself: is this a whole meal, an act, or a time? The answer tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Feeding can be a noun (the act of giving food, a time of eating, or one meal) or a verb form of feed.
fact: The verb forms are feed, feeds, fed and feeding; the past tense of feed is fed.
fact: «Feeding» can mean giving food to a person or animal, or the act of eating.
fact: A feeding is one meal given to a baby or animal, like «the night feeding».
fact: «Feeding the ducks» with bread is not good for them; peas or oats are better.
exercise: «Winter feeding helps small birds survive.» What does feeding mean here? | Flying south for the winter | Building a nest | *Giving food to birds | Singing loudly in the cold
exercise: «...which cuts down fights at feeding time.» What is feeding time? | A time when the animals are asleep | A time when the animals play outside | A time for cleaning the pen | *A time when the animals eat
exercise: A mum says, «Baby's last feeding was at ten o'clock.» What is a feeding here? | *One meal given to the baby | A long walk in the pram | A toy for the baby | The baby's bath time
test: Choose the past tense of feed: «Yesterday the keeper ___ the penguins.» | feeds | feeding | feeder | *fed
test: The zoo sign says «Please do not feed the animals.» Why? | The animals like to be left alone to play | *Human food can make them ill | The animals need to sleep all day | Food is too expensive at the zoo
exam: Read «Cats purr when content, but also when hurt, ill or scared, perhaps to calm themselves; a mother cat purrs while feeding.» Which meaning of feeding fits here? | Growing food in a garden | *The act of eating | Giving food to someone else | Buying food from the shop
